            <p>Extramammary Paget Lesion. The primary lesions of EMPD present as erythematous, scaly plaques that remain well delineated and typically measure several centimeters. Later stages may show crusting, weepy erosions, or ulcerations. Scattered erosions and white scale can produce a classic &#x0201c;strawberries and cream&#x0201d; appearance. <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://dermnetnz.org/images">DermNet New Zealand</ext-link></p>
          </caption>
